For NIL, I might add another layer beyond emotion:

Relational Field

Rather than asking:

“What do I feel?”

or

“What exists externally?”

ask:

“What relationship exists between my internal state and the external world?”

That relationship contains:

* agency
* constraints
* opportunities
* obligations
* social position
* uncertainty
* anticipated futures

Many powerful narratives don’t merely change emotions.

They reorganize this relational field.

A mentor becomes an ally.

A failure becomes training.

A mountain becomes a challenge.

An obstacle becomes a mission.

The external world hasn’t changed.

The relationship has.

